Z||000000||Eric_PA||04-05-2001||11:11 PM||||I set out to install poly bushings in the front of my GT last week and found something causing my front end to be so bad.<P>Take a Look<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mar27$17.jpg">  <BR>As you can see the lower control arm is missing a bit of metal. The whole time I passed it off as being bad bushings. The good thing is that this made me update just about the whole front end with new components. It got new poly, 1" lowering springs and new hardware along with painting the Grand AM brake upgrade that I performed last year. Those calipers rust fast.<P>Eric<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 04-05-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000001||rodmcneill||04-05-2001||11:20 PM||||Wow! I'm glad you discovered that.||||reg||1
